a hang root cause or guarantee1800seconds suffices.\"\n    ],\n    \"base_ci\": \"Parent reports unchanged426 RepositoryChecks run39154122145 success on Linux Python3.13 in~187seconds. Actual workflow independently read: Ubuntu job outertimeout10minutes, Python3.13, bootstrap then managedprepush. Base success is not a check result for this unpublished seven-file batch.\",\n    \"assessment\": \"Observed continued real local progress beyond600seconds on supported-host attempts supports a bounded local full-suite deadline amendment. Static/focused budget and CI outerdeadline can remain independently shorter; timeout duration itself is not an acceptance/quality assertion.\"\n  },\n  \"concrete_plan_assessment\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"agent_tools/workflow.py\",\n      \"assessment\": \"One finite complete-prepush unittest budget changes600\\u21921800. Preserve fixed command list/full discover, existing selection refusal,180static/focused, timeout/returncode failure propagation, private bounded logs, before/after fingerprint and receipt gating. No user-controlled timeout, extra selected profile, partial execution success or bypass is introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"agent_tools/tests/test_workflow.py\",\n      \"assessment\": \"Existing meaningful budget/timeout regression is the appropriate test boundary: assert actual full discover argv with no -p or selected-file flags,180static+1800whole-suite deadlines, actual timedout evidence, no successful receipt and require_checks refusal. Existing bounded focused selection test should additionally assert180deadline and keep focused receipt unable to authorize commit. These avoid sleeping1800seconds while testing the actual command/receipt boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"agent_tools/README.md\",\n      \"assessment\": \"Document whole local suite30minutes versus unchanged180static/focused, complete suite mandatory, no pass receipt on timeout and independent10minute CIouterjob/exactpublishedSHA