_jy_w7/agent_docs/test-matrix.md\",\n      \"bytes\": 7196,\n      \"sha256\": \"a5b2ab4b3cd79f6a25c7103201ee26593c59d7f19d93fba48c25416e5c819c9c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"/private/tmp/atk-pr40-self-host-source-fm_jy_w7/.github/workflows/repository-checks.yml\",\n      \"bytes\": 570,\n      \"sha256\": \"aef054d06bd0dc6e5ac6115f90c6cf4abd46af11676385d597a7cec55598dd51\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"/private/tmp/atk-pr40-self-host-source-fm_jy_w7/.github/required-workflows.json\",\n      \"bytes\": 45,\n      \"sha256\": \"8d14241a212f0e7c09e261913e05c5f401fda8e18364a8329f421bed6f6a176d\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"limits\": \"Read-only independent complete amended-plan/task/source-fact review. No candidate programs/imports/tests/builds/services/scenes/Pi operations, source edits, branches, privateDB writes, posts, approvals, commits/pushes/main/runtime changes. Only this private report written. Plan approval establishes implementable aligned scope, not future source approval, real local/CI success, provenance admission or complete PR40/native/task readiness.\"\n}\n```","Transparent coordinator response after independent full-recorded-task alignment assessment of the exact current question, all three retained answers, original task/correction/replan history and published companion evidence.\n\natk_current_dev_reconciliation: Reconcile dev (Recommended).\n\nReconcile the remaining PR #40 ATK correction against your actual assigned immutable dev 04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9. Preserve both current dev behavior and PR #40's intended resumable independent source review, durable merge exclusion, structured scene findings and recoverable publication. Resolve the real source/test conflicts explicitly in the complete renewed plan; do not choose an entire old or new file indiscriminately. Obtain separate independent complete plan review before coding and fresh exact-head whole-task/source review after publication. This strategy answer approves neither the currently empty complete plan nor code, merge, protected policy, main or runtime activation.\n\nCurrent dev actually adds agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_render.py to protected policy_path and parameterizes both directions of relevant rename coverage. Retain those safeguards and owner/exact-head policy semantics; the session-only automation dev-merge waiver is distinct from changing their implementation or granting main/runtime authority. Retain current dev's coordinator authority/checked-renewal, capture isolation, native/source validation, source-mode isolation, failure-evidence retention, Python-version/runtime-exclusion and other existing safeguards while integrating the PR feature. No baseline467 source diagnostic is production visual acceptance.\n\nPR #40 actually supplies the meaningful readiness correction that current dev still lacks: isolated AGENT_STATE_DIR and complete valid PR identity; a proven healthy ready baseline followed by independent stale-review-base, wrong-App, failed-fast-check and agent:writing cases; plus the isolated integration-nonblocking case. Preserve those cases, exercise the real durable source-review exclusion and retain neighboring source-review/repair-discovery coverage. New bytes require their own actual GitHub matrix, minimum/SDK/quality and aggregate fast-checks; neither historical PR CI nor the companion run substitutes for the changed ATK head. No candidate programs, imports, tests, installs, builds or scenes run on Pi.\n\nThe companion SOURCE leaf is already published at Karapsin/self_host dev 4e90c6ee0b7da8bd436c6efacb03d4a01ce9c2e0, parent4263772ebced62133ad297526f66aed7be1d3c5b, tree783e348477bed8233a6f56bac4e664a3683db9d6. Fresh authenticated reads independently match ALL seven complete published file bodies to the previously independently approved source hashes. Exact push/dev Repository Checks run39247424292 attempt1 is completed success for that exact SHA. This updates source/validation facts; it does not rewrite old pending reports, install the new worker, grant this ATK workspace editable self_host source, release a hold or establish live discovery recovery. The existing supported self_host workflow pushed directly to dev; no companion PR or new publication route is claimed.\n\nPreserve consumed answer6266778719 and its complete inline original delta, instructions, plan/source assessments and actual receipts. Do not repeat the already completed companion source edits inside ATK or ask the owner to upload source/AGENTS. Refresh any truly missing unchanged companion source through the coordinator's existing evidence route and assess actual whole-task/native acceptance separately. Linked/private paths are identifiers, not invented native URL-fetch or repository-switch capabilities. No request/control database mutation is authorized.\n\nThe actual nonproduction source-validation run39250997445 completed on fixed reviewed source2bff and transport/subject467. The coordinator reports all46 full images individually reviewed:41pass/5fail. Those failures remain real; there is no production-correlated receipt or visual approval. Do not substitute that result for PR #40 readiness, changed transport/profile validation, corrected UI acceptance or runtime activation.\n\nRetain the entire original prompt, corrections, questions/options/answers, resolver decisions, plans/checkpoints/replan history, exact source/task/signature/CI bindings and genuine provenance/security/veto/cancel/writer/operational gates. Continue monitoring all qualifying PRs and repair successors through actual successful dev merges; self_host relevance remains GitHub-agent functionality only. Keep ten-worker concurrency, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies with full Q+A, resolver-mediated aligned choices, waiting-agent recovery, singleton30-minute/open-PR orchestration with idle exit and the owner's notification limits. This releases no unrelated hold, claims no resolution of #9 and declares neither PR #40 nor the parent task complete."],"decisions":[{"choice":"readiness_regression_correction: Focused repair (Recommended)\nReason: The readiness tests contain incomplete PR fixtures and lack isolated private state for the negative cases. A healthy baseline followed by independent stale-base, wrong-App, failed-fast-check and agent:writing cases supports the owner's reliable-fix requirement. Preserving the feature and retaining independent companion/whole-task review does not replace the standing objective to monitor all relevant PRs until merged with dev. Validation must run on GitHub after publication; protected exact-head approval remains exclusively with the owner.","questions":["1. For this correction, should the plan repair the confirmed readiness-test gap, preserve the existing PR feature, and leave companion/whole-task review to the independent reviewer?\nFocused repair (Recommended): Use real isolated private state and a valid PR fixture; prove a healthy baseline, then independently test stale base, wrong App, failed fast checks, and agent:writing."]},{"choice":"companion_discovery_correction: Focused inventory repair (Recommended)\nReason: Auditing retained GitHub-agent paths, including test_general_strategy_resolution.py in that audit, and adding independently enumerated discovery cases plus a discovery-to-orchestrator regression supports the requested reliable tooling fix. Excluding unrelated self_host changes follows the owner's relevance restriction. Preserving PR #40's feature and readiness coverage, validating the exact published companion commit on GitHub, and obtaining fresh independent review retains the existing validation requirements. This leaf repair leaves intact monitoring all relevant PRs and resulting repairs until successfully merged with dev, notification restrictions, and owner-only authority. The proposed audit establishes no unverified diagnostic facts or completion claim.","questions":["1. Should this correction repair the companion relevance inventory for verified GitHub-agent regression modules and fixtures in the retained source generations, with independently enumerated discovery cases and a discovery-to-orchestrator regression, while preserving PR #40’s feature and readiness coverage?\nFocused inventory repair (Recommended): Audit actual retained GitHub-agent paths, include test_general_strategy_resolution.py, keep unrelated self_host changes excluded, and validate the exact published companion commit on GitHub before fresh independent review."]},{"choice":"companion_source_assignment: Correct assignment (Recommended)\nReason: Coordinator acquisition of the self_host source, immutable current dev base and repository instructions is an implementation-routing strategy supported by the owner's authorization to fix GitHub-agent tooling in self_host. Fresh planning and separate independent review preserve review requirements without inventing missing source facts. Retain the inventory/test/README/changelog repair, PR #40's existing feature and readiness coverage, exact-published-commit GitHub validation, and all standing requirements, including monitoring every relevant PR through successful dev merge, notification restrictions and owner-only protected approval. This decision establishes neither successful provisioning nor companion revalidation and grants no plan or protected-code approval.","questions":["1. Can the coordinator route this correction to a Karapsin/self_host source assignment with its immutable current dev base and repository instructions, then obtain fresh planning and separate independent plan review? The current assignment exposes analytics_toolkit, so companion revalidation remains unavailable.\nCorrect assignment (Recommended): Coordinator provisions self_host source and base, retains the specified inventory/test/README/changelog repair and all standing requirements, and preserves PR #40’s existing changes."]}],"images":[],"plans":[{"approval_index":null,"id":"59d0caf4fce6270871e8ae306c2bcbc439555df6c27e9f8a40c2063ad79e53c1","text":"# Restore meaningful merge-readiness regression coverage\n\n## Summary\n\nCorrect the confirmed test gap in PR #40 while preserving all existing feature changes. The current head has successful fast CI, but independent review remains rejected and incomplete.\n\nPlanning is grounded in pinned dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`; no code or tests were executed.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Update `tests/repository/github_agent.py::test_stale_review_wrong_app_and_failed_fast_checks_block_merge`.\n- Parameterize four independent cases: stale review base, wrong review App identity, failed fast check, and `agent:writing`.\n- For every case, set `AGENT_STATE_DIR` to `tmp_path`, construct a fresh valid PR using `owned_pr()` with `mergeable=True` and empty labels, and obtain fresh successful checks.\n- Assert that this healthy baseline is ready before changing exactly one condition. Assert that the changed case blocks merging.\n- Exercise the real private-state guard without mocking `source_review.blocks_merge`.\n- Record the correction in `docs/CHANGELOG.md` without changing package versions.\n\nNo production API, schema, controller behavior, dependency, or workflow changes are required. Preserve existing resumable-review changes and Python compatibility.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\n- On GitHub, run the readiness cases plus the existing integration-nonblocking test.\n- Run `tests/repository/github_agent.py` and `tests/repository/source_review.py` to cover neighboring controller behavior and durable review exclusion.\n- Require the existing tests workflow’s matrix, SDK conformance, quality gates, and aggregate `fast-checks` to succeed on the newly published head. Prior-head success is insufficient.\n- Perform no programs, tests, installs, or rendering on RPi.\n- Submit this plan for independent review before implementation. After publication, require fresh independent source review, including the outstanding companion and whole-task assessment.\n- Retain owner-only exact-head protected-policy approval for the complete PR; the resolver decision grants neither plan nor policy approval.\n\n## Completion and standing requirements\n\n- Revalidate against current dev before implementation; materially changed scope requires independent plan review.\n- Preserve `agent:writing` lifecycle handling and the original chronological task context, including questions, resolver choices, and their distinct authority.\n- The controller/coordinator continues monitoring all relevant PRs and resulting repairs until successfully merged with dev. Include `self_host` PRs only when they affect GitHub-agent functionality.\n- Restrict owner notifications to approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases, and main merges.\n- This correction does not establish that the broader task is complete or that the orchestrator has resolved #9.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"d8abc85da089180cc5af5678103c7f5577b797411dd1e08db128890e6cb65da6","text":"# Reconcile PR #40 with current dev and renew independent review\n\n## Summary\n\nReconcile PR head `b0dc9cd6324565f5931cdab894d572830ec22d5f` with assigned immutable dev `04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9`. Preserve PR #40’s resumable source review, durable merge exclusion, structured scene findings, recoverable publication, and corrected readiness tests while retaining later dev safeguards.\n\nThe complete refreshed feedback export includes both coordinator responses. Historical PR fast checks passed; independent review remains incomplete. The companion source correction is reported published at `self_host` commit `4e90c6ee0b7da8bd436c6efacb03d4a01ce9c2e0`, with exact-commit Repository Checks success. Do not repeat those source edits in ATK.\n\nSubmit this complete reconciliation plan for separate independent review before coding. No files changed or candidate programs executed during planning.\n\n## Implementation and conflict resolution\n\n### Controller and review protocol\n\n- Integrate the PR’s additive controller interfaces: protocol selection, review progress, immutable bundle binding, required evidence, and generation replacement. Retain the optional `source_protocol` keyword on `prepare`; preserve existing callers.\n- Keep pending-review handling in discovery, the real durable exclusion in `ready`, and typed pending/terminal handling in publication.\n- Preserve dev’s exact visual-renderer entry in `policy_path`, including owner-only exact-head semantics and both rename endpoints.\n- Retain `.github/agent/source_review.py`, its source/scene schemas, and source-review prompt. Preserve immutable assignment identities, complete coverage requirements, concrete findings, compare-and-set generation replacement, and recovery of accepted publication side effects.\n- Keep legacy or incomplete assessments pending. Neither retrieved pages nor historical approvals establish complete source review.\n- Preserve dev’s `review_control` coordinator loader, snapshot/checked-renewal APIs, and checked-receipt table. The source-review tables remain additive; do not replace existing tables, migrate private state manually, or clear holds.\n\n### Preserve later dev safeguards\n\nResolve these differences by retaining dev behavior; the PR feature requires no reversal of them:\n\n- Coordinator authority, contract, snapshot, and transition modules, their support fixtures, and their regression coverage.\n- Capture isolation, sandbox, native probe, source-validation implementation, failure diagnostics, and associated tests.\n- `.github/workflows/agent-visual.yml` isolation and diagnostic handling.\n- `.github/workflows/tests.yml` separate source-validation/probe modes, mode-specific check identities, and exclusion from ordinary successful `fast-checks`.\n- MCP source/toolchain drift checks and receipt certification; retain neighboring check-drift regressions.\n- Python 3.9–3.14 runtime profiles, `py39-min`, minimum-constraint validation and `pip check`. Preserve the Python 3.8 public/static compatibility floor without reinstating Python 3.8 runtime jobs.\n- Existing dependency constraints, release-check tooling, immutable task-evidence records, and unrelated changes already present on dev.\n\nDo not resolve shared files by selecting an entire old or new version without checking their individual changes.\n\n### Tests and documentation\n\n- In `tests/repository/github_agent.py`, combine the PR’s valid repository/PR fixtures and isolated `AGENT_STATE_DIR` with dev’s expanded protected-path rename tests.\n- Retain all four independent readiness cases: prove a healthy ready baseline, change exactly one of stale review base, wrong App, failed fast check, or `agent:writing`, then assert refusal.\n- Preserve the isolated integration-nonblocking case. Do not mock `source_review.blocks_merge` in readiness tests.\n- Keep the source-review tests and narrowly scoped pending-review fakes used by unrelated discovery fixtures.\n- In `agent_tools/README.md`, retain the resumable-review documentation addition while preserving dev’s validation, receipt-drift, Python-profile, and dependency guidance.\n- Preserve all current operational documentation. Merge changelog entries additively, retaining dev history and recording the feature/readiness reconciliation without changing package versions.\n\n## Compatibility and focused regression coverage\n\nNo public toolkit API or dependency expansion is required. The review interfaces and private tables are additive; existing coordinator contracts and ordinary controller calls remain compatible.\n\nRun focused tests on GitHub using disposable private state and fake external services:\n\n- Readiness baseline and four blocking cases; integration remains nonblocking.\n- Durable pending review across restart/base changes, stale generation refusal, complete coverage admission, and legacy/incomplete disposition.\n- Terminal publication retry after accepted check, review, correction, or notification responses are lost; preserve later findings, vetoes, and coordinator holds.\n- Add one coexistence regression using the real control database: source-review initialization and completion preserve checked-renewal records and existing control barriers.\n- Retain and run neighboring repair-discovery, coordinator authority/checked-renewal, protected-path/rename, automation-promotion, capture isolation, native/source-validation, MCP check-drift, and Python-profile regressions.\n\nUse the existing suites rather than adding tests that merely duplicate implementation structure. Execute no programs, imports, tests, installs, builds, or scenes on Pi.\n\n## GitHub validation and independent acceptance\n\n- Before implementation, refresh the actual assignment’s head/base and writer ownership through the coordinator. Material differences from this plan require renewed independent plan review.\n- Publish through the existing signed correction lifecycle, preserving complete chronological task context, questions/options/answers, resolver decisions, checkpoints, and source generations.\n- Require the resulting exact ATK head to pass Python 3.9–3.14 tests, `py39-min` with `pip check`, both SDK profiles, quality/coverage/artifact gates, and aggregate ordinary `fast-checks`. Historical PR or companion success cannot validate new ATK bytes.\n- Obtain fresh independent complete source and whole-task review bound to the resulting head, current dev base, and task digest.\n- For companion assessment, use the published `4e90c6…` delta and actual receipts. Any genuinely required unchanged source must be fetched and assigned by the coordinator through the existing immutable evidence route.\n- Keep source publication, selected worker generation, runtime activation, and live recovery as distinct facts. The reported nonproduction capture’s five failed images remain failures; its 41 passing images do not establish production visual acceptance.\n- Preserve genuine signature, provenance, security, ownership, cancellation, veto, and protected-policy checks. Apply only independently verified, applicable session waivers; never change their implementation or infer main/runtime permission.\n\n## Standing completion obligations\n\nThe coordinator/controller continues monitoring every qualifying PR and repair successor through successful dev merge and required post-merge repair. Include `self_host` PRs only when they affect GitHub-agent functionality.\n\nRetain ten workers, truthful lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, resolver-mediated aligned choices, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies with complete Q&A, waiting-agent recovery, singleton 30-minute orchestration while qualifying PRs are open, and idle exit.\n\nOwner notifications remain restricted to approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases, and main merges. This ATK correction grants no runtime activation, main promotion, unrelated hold release, or claim that issue #9 or the parent task is complete.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:68302ba1bca84a8691e7576dffd2f5cb","questions":[{"answer_index":18,"id":"aa1bc3e0576cfbbd385e0474bf6d73d151ed7d3c1d4f5a16d73c56958efd02a9","text":"Planning remains blocked by the source assignment. The assigned repository is `analytics_toolkit`; `self_host` source and its immutable current dev base are unavailable. No files changed or programs executed.\n\nI read all bound current-head check and feedback pages. PR #40’s fast checks succeed; independent review remains rejected and incomplete. The later routing decision does not prove provisioning occurred.\n\n1. **Coordinator:** Can you complete the already-selected `Karapsin/self_host` assignment and expose its source, immutable current dev base, and repository instructions for fresh planning and separate independent plan review?\n\nThe retained correction covers the relevance inventory, independent discovery cases, rename and scheduling regressions, README maintenance guidance, and task changelog fragment. Preserve PR #40’s feature/readiness changes and all standing monitoring and approval requirements. No additional owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":19,"id":"e53beb7b0408674c7febf3578919a9864c98fe8835f00285c695d438484d0e05","text":"1. Should the revised correction reconcile PR #40 with pinned dev 04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9, preserving newer dev safeguards—including visual-renderer protected approval and rename coverage—alongside the existing resumable-review feature and readiness tests, then obtain separate independent plan review?\nReconcile dev (Recommended): Retain current dev behavior and PR #40’s intended additions; review material conflicts independently and validate the resulting exact head on GitHub."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"implement it on your own if orchestator is not doing that","task_id":"68302ba1bca84a8691e7576dffd2f5cb","version":2}